WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:05.310
There is a very interesting new poll from
The Wall Street Journal about this upcoming

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:06.310
election.

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:09.620
And it's interesting not because it says Biden
is ahead by nine.

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:11.120
We have many polls that say that.

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:17.060
And it may be true if we see the margin of
error, Biden plus nine might really mean Biden

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:18.110
plus two.

00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:19.520
That's nothing new here.

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:25.770
What's interesting about this new poll is
that it breaks down Trump vs. Biden all along

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:27.930
a number of different voting groups.

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:32.440
And when you look at it, when you slice and
dice the electorate, you see that Donald Trump

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:36.149
is winning among men, barely 47 43.

00:00:36.149 --> 00:00:39.460
That's interesting because Republicans tend
to win among men by more than four points.

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:42.410
We'll talk about that more on Friday.

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:43.410
Trump is winning among.

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:46.989
White voters, barely 49 to 47.

00:00:46.989 --> 00:00:52.100
And Donald Trump is winning among people with
high school or less education by a huge margin,

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:53.420
nearly 20 points.

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:58.420
Trump is up 54 36 among what are colloquially
called the uneducated.

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:01.899
Now, every other group, every single other
group.

00:01:01.899 --> 00:01:03.749
Donald Trump is losing.

00:01:03.749 --> 00:01:05.980
Some examples include black voters.

00:01:05.980 --> 00:01:08.000
Biden's up 88 to 80.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.030
Brutal people with postgraduate degrees.

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:13.700
Biden is up 65 to 28.

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:15.150
People who are college graduates.

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:17.410
Biden is up 61 31.

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:22.210
Among women and among Hispanic voters, Biden
has 57 percent support.

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:27.190
And importantly, among independents, Biden
is up 24, 49 to 25.

00:01:27.190 --> 00:01:32.640
Now, when you see this, you have to consider
whether some of these things are cadge, are

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:34.670
causal or correlated.

00:01:34.670 --> 00:01:40.030
So, for example, the more education you have,
the more likely you are to vote Biden.

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:41.030
We see that right.

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:42.560
High school or less.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:46.080
Biden has 36 supports, sir, 36 percent support.

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:47.850
If you have some college.

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:49.780
Biden has 47 percent support.

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:51.510
Few graduated college.

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:53.630
Biden support goes up to 61.

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:57.700
And if you have a post graduate degree, Biden
is up even higher to 67.

00:01:57.700 --> 00:01:59.710
I believe this is causal.

00:01:59.710 --> 00:02:01.600
I don't think this is merely correlation.

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:08.550
Donald Trump's campaign has been objectively
one of lying to voters about things he could

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:11.499
never possibly do as president.

00:02:11.499 --> 00:02:14.799
And many people fell for voting for Trump.

00:02:14.799 --> 00:02:16.090
That's the right terminology.

00:02:16.090 --> 00:02:18.209
Not everybody, but many people did.

00:02:18.209 --> 00:02:23.209
More education makes you less likely to vote
for a candidate like Trump.

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:25.690
And I would argue for Republicans more broadly.

00:02:25.690 --> 00:02:31.510
So in this case, if you want people to vote
for Trump, you actually benefit from hurting

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:35.939
education, not funding public schools, not
dealing with the student lending crisis.

00:02:35.939 --> 00:02:36.959
So on and so forth.

00:02:36.959 --> 00:02:41.750
So you really have to look at this stuff and
understand the link to campaign strategy and

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:42.780
platforms.

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:47.980
There are ideologically based positions that
politicians will take or parties will go in

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:49.219
the direction of.

00:02:49.219 --> 00:02:52.829
But there are also self-preservation directions.

00:02:52.829 --> 00:02:59.180
Are Republicans against education because
some of them see it as anti religious indoctrination?

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:00.180
Sure.

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:01.180
Yeah.

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:02.760
That exists among some right wing voters.

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:07.140
But a lot of right wing voters recognize that
the more educated people are, the less likely

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:08.140
they are to vote for them.

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:10.069
And so that's really important to look at.

00:03:10.069 --> 00:03:12.700
Now, one last word of caution.

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:20.590
Biden plus nine in this poll, two and a half
months before the election is exactly where

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:27.659
Hillary Clinton was in this poll two and a
half months before the 2016 election.

00:03:27.659 --> 00:03:29.299
That's all that needs to be said.

00:03:29.299 --> 00:03:36.029
Trust nothing other than your ability to vote
and to convince others to vote.

00:03:36.029 --> 00:03:37.180
That's it.

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:42.739
We are coming up on the David Pakman shows,
15th anniversary on August.

00:03:42.739 --> 00:03:44.760
Twenty third on that day.

